# Workbench watchdog checks. One check per line; blank lines and # ignored.
#
#   unit       <systemd-unit>                  system unit must be active
#   user       <systemd-unit>                  --user unit must be active
#   heartbeat  <label> <file> <max-age-secs>   file must exist and be fresh
#   net        <host>                          host must answer ping
#   disk       <mountpoint> <min-free-pct>     free space floor
#
# Units that are not installed yet are reported as MISSING, not FAILED, so this
# file can list Phase 2+ services before they exist.

net        1.1.1.1
disk       /            10

# The phone's view of this machine. If this timer dies, STATUS.md silently goes
# stale and everything looks fine from outside — so watch it explicitly.
user       workbench-status.timer
user       workbench-watchdog.timer

# --- Phase 2: installed 2026-07-22 ---
unit       ollama.service
unit       tailscaled.service

# --- Phase 4: scraper jobs write their marker file on each successful run ---
# heartbeat dba-scraper    /home/lukashoerup/.local/state/workbench/heartbeats/dba      7200
# heartbeat vinted-scraper /home/lukashoerup/.local/state/workbench/heartbeats/vinted   7200
# heartbeat nightly-triage /home/lukashoerup/.local/state/workbench/heartbeats/triage  100000
